  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-06-29T22:06:13.581Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Multiple Oculus audio scripts were removed from the dependencies folder of VRChat's SDK in this version.\n\nOne of the removed scripts was `ONSP Ambisonics Native` -- this script was historically required to decode ambisonic audio properly alongside Unity's native support. [It seems to still be the case according to the Oculus docs.](https://developer.oculus.com/documentation/audiosdk/latest/concepts/ospnative-unity-ambisonic/#add-ambisonic-audio-to-a-unity-scene)\n\nI'm unsure of how many world creators are currently using ambisonics in their world, but removing this script could result in some audio chaos when they update their world with the new SDK. The ability to have ambisonic audio in worlds should remain either way! \n\nIf anyone is unsure of what ambisonics is, it basically allows you to create a sphere of 3D audio packed into a single audio file. It's becoming a standard format in VR for looping ambient environment sounds, music cues, etc. [Here's some other nerd info on it!](https://www.waves.com/ambisonics-explained-guide-for-sound-engineers)",
